 ## Overview
-Axis Threshold Clipping is a dynamic clipping method for 3D Gaussian Splatting that discards Gaussians whose projected screen-space bounding quad exceeds a maximum axis length threshold $\tau_\lambda$ [S1]. It solves the performance bottleneck of processing large, distant Gaussians that fall outside the view frustum but have significant screen-space extent, specifically targeting mobile hardware constraints [S1]. It differs from sibling dynamic clipping techniques by using a simple axis-aligned bound check on the projected quad rather than complex frustum intersection tests [S1].
